  "id": "deadspaceinteriors",
  "neon": "#4affd0",
  "note": "A furniture showroom, so the upper floor is the display case: a square volume with a second one turned twenty-four degrees through it, which gives the room behind the glass eight corners to light and reads as a lantern over the street after dark. Its neon moved off the old flat green onto the cyan-green the clinical family burns, which is what the rest of the west is lit in now. ⚠ A CANTILEVER AND A ROTATION NEVER SHARE A SEGMENT — see the warning in aurelia.json. An offset box and a yawed box are each safe; a box that is both puts the derived kit where its own solid is not, and glself catches it. So asymmetry here is offset-only and every chamfer is CENTRED. RENDER_TUNE.legacyArms puts the showroom arm back.",
